# First answer

## Section

Define one AI Agent and ask one question. The default path uses a local MockLLM
server. Change only `backend` to `:live` to use the model in the Agent definition.
Live mode needs `OPENAI_API_KEY`. Run the cells in order from this checkout.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

mock =
  if backend == :mock do
    {:ok, pid} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: [%{reply: {:text, "Ready"}}])
    pid
  end

context =
  if mock do
    %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}
  else
    %{}
  end
```

The mock changes the model transport only. The request still uses ReqLLM,
Jido Flow, and AgentServer.

## Define the Agent

```elixir
defmodule Guide.FirstAnswer do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_first_answer"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("")})

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Answer in one short sentence."

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
        max_model_calls 1
      end

      result into: :answer
    end
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/ai/first_answer"

    route "guides.ai.first_answer", ai: :assistant do
      define :answer, args: [:query]
    end
  end
end
```

The `ai` block describes the request. `result into:` stores the final answer
in the Agent's domain state. The route lets the generated `ask_sync/3` helper
submit the request.

## Ask and inspect

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.FirstAnswer, id: "guide-first-answer")
{:ok, answer} = Guide.FirstAnswer.ask_sync(server, "Say you are ready.", context: context)
state = Jido.AgentServer.agent(server).state

%{answer: answer, stored_answer: state.answer}
```

In mock mode, both answers are `"Ready"`. In live mode, the wording can vary.
The completed request is not the same as the short AgentServer admission Turn.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: []} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)
end

:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Continue with [Three tool rounds](three_tool_rounds.livemd) or read
[Your first AI agent](../v3/01_first_agent.md).

